-- TESTS for the references.  Hand counts from the Wikisource text of the Basic Law: nine `ח:הערה` notes carrying eleven link targets (s 1: 2, s 2: 1, s 3: 1, s 4: 1,
-- s 5: 1, s 8: 1, s 9(a): 1, s 9(b): 2, s 10: 1).  None is in the official page (read from the page image of Sefer HaChukim 2743 p. 898).
-- Expected-red checks (the flag colour words, the count in article 82) are in il40-tests-expected-red.l4.

§ `Tests: references`

#ASSERT count `the pointers the consolidation prints` EQUALS 11
#ASSERT NOT (any `the pointer is in the official text:` `the pointers the consolidation prints`)
#ASSERT `the words of s 3` EQUALS `the words of s 1 of Basic Law: Jerusalem, Capital of Israel`
-- Section 9(b)'s names are spelled with a plene yod (זיכרון) where the Memorial Day Law's own title has none (זכרון): the same day, two spellings.
#ASSERT NOT (`the name s 9(b) gives the first memorial day` EQUALS `the Memorial Day Law's own wording of that name`)
-- Section 2(b) and the Declaration agree on what the two descriptions share: the stripes are blue in both (the colour words differ: see the expected-red file).
#ASSERT `s 2(b) describes the flag's colours as`'s `the colour word for the two stripes` EQUALS "תכלת"
#ASSERT `the Declaration of 28 October 1948 describes the flag's colours as`'s `the colour word for the two stripes` EQUALS "תכלת כהה"
#ASSERT `s 2(b) describes the flag's colours as`'s `the colour word for the Magen David` EQUALS "תכול"
#ASSERT `the Declaration of 28 October 1948 describes the flag's colours as`'s `the colour word for the Magen David` EQUALS "תכלת"
